    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/beet_salad_with_feta?rev=1607803448&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-12-12T15:04:08-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:beet_salad_with_feta - created</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/beet_salad_with_feta?rev=1607803448&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Beet salad with Feta, from William Sonoma's “Mediterranean Cooking”,1997; recipes by Joyce Goldstein.

Ingredients:

	*  4 large or 8 small beets
	*  1/2 cup extra-virgin olive oil
	*  3 tablespoons red wine vinegar (or 1.4 cup fresh lemon juice)
	*  1 clove garlic, minced
	*  [1/2 cup chopped fresh mint, for vinaigrette]
	*  1/2 teaspoon ground allspice
	*  1 red onion, thinly sliced
	*  6-7 oz watercress or lettuce mix or spinach, washed and stemmed
	*  1 cup crumbled feta cheese</description>
    </item>
