        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:beefy_mushroom_barley_soup - created</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/beefy_mushroom_barley_soup?rev=1607802014&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Beefy Mushroom Barley Soup
from: Penzey's Spices

Ingredients:

	*  1 lb lean beef chuck (beef stew meat), cut into 1 inch cubes
	*  2 tablespoons olive oil
	*  3 medium or 2 large onions, coarsely chopped
	*  10 oz fresh mushrooms, sliced
	*  3 large carrots, sliced
	*  1/2 cup pearl barley
	*  7 cups beef broth (I used 1 4 cup container of beef brother and 3 cups water mixed with Penzey's beef base for 1 cup)
	*  1 cup dry red wine (or tomato juice)
	*  Salt and pepper to taste (instead, I use…</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/chili?rev=1605883659&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-11-20T09:47:39-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>faith</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:chili - created</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/chili?rev=1605883659&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>These recipes are all based on Rik's Mom's Chili recipe.

Original



	*  1/2 pound, ground chuck
	*  chopped onion
	*  8oz tomato sauce
	*  1 can tomato soup
	*  15oz red kidney beans
	*  1 tsp flour
	*  2-3 tsp chili powder
	*  1 tsp brown sugar
	*  cook 25 minutes</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/deviled_eggs?rev=1605823750&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-11-19T17:09:10-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:deviled_eggs</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/deviled_eggs?rev=1605823750&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Deviled eggs, variations.

1.Cover 1 dozen eggs with water and bring to a boil. Turn to low and let sit for 15 minutes. Turn off heat, let sit for 10 minutes, then drain water.
2. Peel eggs, cut in half lengthwise and remove all yolks.
3. Add yolks to bowl along with 1/4 cup mayonnaise.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/best_low-carb_coleslaw?rev=1605745239&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-11-18T19:20:39-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:best_low-carb_coleslaw - created</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/best_low-carb_coleslaw?rev=1605745239&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Best Low-carb Coleslaw (Food.com)

	*  16 ounces shredded cabbage (about 1 small to medium cabbage)
	*  1 small onion, thinly sliced
	*  1/4 cup Splenda
	*  1/2 teaspoon salt
	*  1/2 teaspoon fresh ground black pepper
	*  1/2 cup mayonnaise
	*  1/2 cup whipping cream OR half-and-half OR buttermilk OR plain kefir
	*  1 1/2 tablespoons white vinegar
	*  2 1/2 tablespoons lemon juice</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/garden/plantings?rev=1604797852&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-11-07T20:10:52-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:plantings - [2019] </title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/garden/plantings?rev=1604797852&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>2007 or 2008: Corylus avellana 'contorted', “Harry lauder's Walking stick”, by garage, next to walkway to garden.
2007 or 2008, planted 2 Honeysuckle,”halls”, on either side of back porch stairs. (Direct Gardening). By 2009, they are covering the trellises there and are cold hardy. Many perfumed flowers in Spring.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/garden/garden?rev=1602175124&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-10-08T12:38:44-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:garden - [GARDEN 2018] </title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/garden/garden?rev=1602175124&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Raised Beds 2007:
Bed 1, near garage, near house:
Tomatoes Brandywine, (Seeds of Change). Grew well, many tomatoes initially, then with drought, had problems with decreased production and blossom end rot. Note:  leave more room for plants and stake them well.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/garden/orchard?rev=1600655808&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-09-20T22:36:48-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:orchard</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/garden/orchard?rev=1600655808&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>04-07  planted Dwarf Patio Peach in contained round bed by garage, surrounded by mints.
( Peach: dwarf ornamental form with double pink flowers; fruit is red/gold with small white-fleshed freestone. Leaves are long slender brilliant reddish purple throughout the season. Deciduous. Useful as accent or container plant. Hardiness zone 5-9. grown by Holland Nursery, Franklin, VA 23851.  Bought at Harris teeter, Chapel Hill, $29.99.)</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/bisquick_substitute?rev=1599346828&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-09-05T19:00:28-05:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>mcf</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:bisquick_substitute - created</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/bisquick_substitute?rev=1599346828&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Bisquick® Substitute
Yield: 1 cup

INGREDIENTS
1 cup all-purpose flour
1 ½ teaspoons baking powder
¼ teaspoon salt
1 tablespoon butter

Step 1
Sift flour into a bowl; add baking powder and salt and whisk until fully incorporated. Cut butter into flour mixture using a pastry cutter until evenly combined.
Shortening or oil can be used in place of the butter, if desired. If using melted butter, be sure to evenly disperse the butter as much as possible.</description>
    </item>
